16 0 obj
<< /A 62 0 R /Alt (PRISMA flowchart illustrating study selection for a review, showing identification of 832 records, exclusion reasons, screening of 430 records, eligibility assessment of 234, and final inclusion of 142 studies.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 63 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a pie chart showing proportions of studies by disease category; panel B features a stacked bar chart comparing the number of studies per omics type and disease; panel C is a horizontal bar chart summarizing participant cohort sizes; panel D is a vertical bar chart depicting publication count per year; panel E is a bar chart illustrating study distribution by country; panel F is a bar chart comparing analytical techniques used; panel G presents violin plots showing percentage of males in  ME/CFS, PACS and respective control groups; panel H shows violin plots of mean age across the same four groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 64 0 R /Alt (Table displaying GRADE assessment across included studies in multiple columns with color-coded cells in green, yellow, and red. Columns correspond to reference, PMID, imprecision, inconsistencies, risk of bias, initial score, penalties, and final score. The data is organized into four vertical segments. Most studies show a moderate concern of imprecision as indicated by yellow highlighting, low to moderate concern of inconsistencies, indicated by mostly green and yellow cells, and high concern of risk of bias, indicated by many red cells. Final scores show overall low to moderate uncertainty of evidence \(green or yellow\), with some scores highlighted in red to indicate strong concerns. ) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 65 0 R /Alt (Four bar charts display the distribution of Newcastle-Ottawa Scale \(NOS\) scores across included studies. Chart A shows selection criteria, with most studies scoring two to four stars. Chart B presents comparability, with the majority receiving zero stars. Chart C covers exposure or outcome, with most studies earning zero stars. Chart D illustrates total NOS scores, with most studies scoring four stars and very few achieving high total scores.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 66 0 R /Alt (Table displaying NOS assessment across included studies in multiple columns with color-coded cells in green, yellow, and red. Columns correspond to reference, PMID, selection, comparability, exposure or outcome, and the overall NOS score. The data is organized into four vertical segments. Most studies show a high risk of bias as indicated by mostly red color-coding. Of the three criteria, selection has the lowest risk of bias as indicated by mostly green or yellow cells, while only some studies show low or moderate risk in comparability and even fewer in exposure/outcome.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 67 0 R /Alt (Metabolic pathway diagram illustrating amino acid metabolism, including tryptophan\220s role in neurotransmitter production, kynurenine pathway neurotoxicity, TCA cycle intermediates, ATP synthesis, and synthesis of nucleotides, lipids, cholesterol, glutathione, and extracellular matrix for redox homeostasis and cellular functions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
